Package: corne-arcane-host
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.10),
         python3-gi,
         dbus-user-session
Suggests: x11-utils
Description: privacy-redacted desktop semantics for a Corne Arcane keyboard
 Sends bounded desktop and browser activity semantics to a Corne v3 RP2040
 keyboard running the griffin_arcane firmware, over QMK Raw HID. The keyboard
 is fully functional without this package; it only enriches what the OLEDs
 show.
 .
 Adapters report enums, durations, counters and salted digests. Window titles,
 URLs, page content, command text, file paths and typed text are never read
 into retained state and have no path onto either wire protocol. A missing bus,
 denied permission or absent extension disables only that one adapter.
 .
 Focus reporting needs a producer. GNOME Shell 45 or newer and KWin under
 Plasma 6 are supported; on other desktops focus semantics stay at their
 default and everything else still works. dbus-user-session is required
 because the daemon runs as a D-Bus-activated systemd user service.
